# Porting

Run the driver on a new MCU by writing one class: the port.

<!-- generated: datasheet-refs -->
<!-- /generated -->

The driver calls hooks on a class you derive from `xmpl100::SpiInterface<Self>` (in
[`inc/xmpl100_spi_interface.hpp`](../inc/xmpl100_spi_interface.hpp)). The base declares no hook; the driver template
is constrained by the `xmpl100::SpiPort` concept, so a missing or misdeclared hook is a compile error.

## What you implement

| Method | Required | Contract |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `bool EnsureInitialized() noexcept` | yes | Bring the ADC up on the first call; `true` at once afterwards |
| `bool ReadVoltageMv(uint8_t channel, uint32_t& voltage_mv) noexcept` | yes | One calibrated conversion in millivolts; `false` on an error |
| `void DelayUs(uint32_t us) noexcept` | yes, for every wait | Wait at least `us` microseconds |
| `bool GpioSet(CtrlPin, GpioSignal) noexcept` | no | Drive SHDN_N; without it `Sleep()` returns `Unsupported` |
| `void Log(LogLevel, const char* message) noexcept` | no | Print one line; `message` is plain text, never a format string |

